## The condition this archive has to meet, in the publisher's words

The same terms carry an obligation aimed directly at anyone republishing
ratings:

> "The ratings are subject to change as they are regularly updated to reflect
> the standards found when a business is inspected by a local authority food
> safety officer. Users are reminded that displaying or otherwise using an
> invalid or inaccurate rating may constitute a criminal offence and/or expose
> the user to potential civil liability. **It is the responsibility of users to
> ensure that the current rating is used or to indicate the date when the
> information was updated.**"

This repository publishes ratings that are deliberately **not** current — that
is its entire purpose — so it takes the second option, everywhere and without
exception:

- every observation carries `observed_at`, set to the **`ExtractDate` the FSA
  stamped on the file**, not the time we fetched it;
- every establishment carries `rating_date`, the date the rating was given;
- every chart states the capture it was drawn from.

**This is not a current-ratings service and must not be used as one.** For the
rating that applies to a business today, go to
[ratings.food.gov.uk](https://ratings.food.gov.uk). Where that site and this
archive disagree, the FSA is right and this is stale.

